 lower level provides an expansive rumpus room with a wet bar, full bathroom, dedicated laundry, and direct access to the backyard patio?ideal for entertaining or casual indoor-outdoor living. Set on a sprawling 9,056-square-foot lot, the private backyard is a lush oasis with ample possibilities for entertaining, gardening, play, or future enhancements. Built in 1964, the home embodies mid-century character while offering tremendous opportunity for modern updates or personalization. Nestled on a quiet residential street, this property enjoys proximity to scenic hiking trails, highly regarded schools within the Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified School District, and convenient access to shopping, dining, and scenic coastal drives?all while providing an oasis of privacy and tranquility. With a unique legacy of loving stewardship and exceptional long-term value, this elegant Rancho Palos Verdes home invites you to continue its story in one of the Peninsula?s most desirable communities. Don?t miss the opportunity to make it your own.","","All Bedrooms Up, Family Room, Living Room","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Vista Grande","Palos Verdes Peninsula","Ridgecrest","","Dana","Ben-Yehuda","CLW-C140262","CLW-X79013","","","The Agency","1600000","False","Full Service","Property is vacant. Go direct. Supra on front door.","True","None","False","","2108","Assessor","","CA","Closed","Multi/Split ","","","San Nicolas","","27914","","","","Cash to New Loan","","25107","","Single Family Residence","","","Neighborhood","True","","","","1964","90275","",""
