 timeless residence nestled in the enchanting Blackhorse area of Rancho Palos Verdes. Starting with the home's front door facing the southern side of the house, receiving abundant natural sunlight and warmth throughout the day. This classic 4-bedroom, 3-bathroom home is a story of elegance and charm, sprawled across a generous 18,448-square-foot lot. Stepping inside, you're greeted by a stunning sunlit kitchen, featuring a cozy breakfast counter that beckons for morning coffee rituals. As the heart of the home, the living room exudes warmth with its inviting fireplace, perfect for relaxing as the sun sets and its glow dances off the hardwood floors. Its open concept allows for everyone to enjoy each other's company. Two sets of French doors open onto two decks?a sanctuary of tranquility that offers breathtaking views of the canyon and the glittering lights of Downtown Los Angeles. Ascending to the second level, you?ll find four bedrooms, each a serene retreat promising restful nights. Two of the bedrooms share a wonderful balcony that overlooks city lights. The primary suite is a haven with its incredible panoramic views that stretch as far as the eye can see, making it an ideal spot for twilight reflections. You will find a step down fifth bedroom that will be perfect as a work office, guest room, family room, or a second primary bedroom with access to the homes second private deck. Outside, the 2-car attached garage provides convenience with your own personal Testla charger, while the peaceful neighborhood envelops you in its beauty and serenity. The home's proximity to Soleado Elementary and Peninsula High School offers top-rated education, and nearby Bristol Farms, Equinox, Regal Cinema, Pen Shopping Center, and various restaurants ensure that all your needs are just moments away. Beyond its scenic city and mountain views and meticulously crafted interior, this home boasts a newer roof in 2021, modern amenities such as free and clear solar panels, a tankless water heater, and a HALO water softener, enhancing its luxurious and comfortable lifestyle. In addition to its many features, this home boasts a charming variety of fruit trees, including pomegranate, guava, fig, apricot, apple, plum, lemon, and more. Imagine enjoying fresh fruit from your own backyard, adding a delightful touch to your everyday living experience. Welcome to your next chapter. Do not hesitate because this good luck charm will be gone soon.","Shingle","Multi-Level Bedroom, Walk-In Closet","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Soleado","Palos Verdes Peninsula","Ridgecrest","","Linlin","Caldwell","TRCALDLIN","PB2088","","","Star Max Realty","1762000","False","Full Service","Please text me  your business card with DRE# required to make an appointment. Will need at least one hour in advance notice. Do not just show up as you will need  CBS code that will be given when making the appointment. Easy to show. Feel free to call for any questions. Call for further details. A fast escrow is encouraged but all offers will be considered. NOTE: The sellers may have the home painted inside prior to the close of escrow. DO NOT USE SHOWTIME.","True","None","False","","2148","Assessor","","CA","Closed","Two, Multi/Split ","","","Browndeer","","4903","Lane","","Ranch, Traditional","Cash, Cash to New Loan, Conventional","","27980","","Single Family Residence","","Electricity Connected, Natural Gas Connected, Phone Available, Sewer Connected","City Lights, Mountain(s)","True","","","Double Pane Windows","1965","90275","3917","RPRS10000-OH*"
