se","","964.02","PRICE REDUCED! Sweeping views. Mid-century aesthetic. Mature fruit trees . . . All the magic of Palos Verdes wrapped up in a pint-sized property. Peep through the picture window, enter the white picket-fenced rose bush-filled front yard and pass the inviting bench on the covered porch. Open your front door to be greeted by sweeping views of the South Bay. Follow the view to an expansive (450+ sf) deck conveniently located adjacent to the kitchen, providing ample private space for entertaining amidst the treetops and chirping birds.  Inside, upgraded wood floors gleam in the living room, while the carpeted bonus area invites cozy relaxation. A privacy curtain easily converts this large space to a third sleeping area for visiting guests. Relax with morning coffee and rest your eyes on the attractively landscaped front yard garden in the picture-perfect bay window. Sliding glass doors showcase the trickling fountain. The galley kitchen further embraces the view while providing convenient space for family meals. Ready to party? Set up the bar in the kitchen and your guests will easily flow through to the deck for sunset cocktails.  Shiplap walls and recessed storage niches in the remodeled bathroom evoke the charm of a traditional era, while the step-in shower enables multi-generational accessibility. The 400sf (btv) garage has multiple windows that continue to leverage the view, making it an ideal space for a home office, work shop, or whatever use suits your lifestyle.  While this traditional home is fully accessible at street level, the double-sized lot is gracefully terraced in the rear. The property leverages this unique feature with a stone-lined trail that connects multiple flat pads, inviting garden parties, exploration and play. The home's interior and exterior layout works for entertaining groups both large and intimate, while more than 20 mature fruit trees and bougainvillea check all the boxes for the ultimate California lifestyle.  With a Walkscore of 68, 1939 Jaybrook Drive combines the convenience of living in town with the lifestyle of the country: it is a 2-minute drive to Trader Joe?s, yet less than a one-mile walk to the extensive trail network of the Miraleste area of Rancho Palos Verdes.","","All Bedrooms Down, Bonus Room, Family Room, Galley Kitchen","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Dapplegray","Palos Verdes Peninsula","Miraleste","","Terri","Harkins","SHARKTER","S1092","","","Vista Sotheby's International Realty","1045000","False","Full Service","n/a","True","None","False","True","1084","Assessor","","CA","Closed","One","","","Jaybrook Drive","","1939","","","Traditional","Conventional","","16010","","Single Family Residence","","","City Lights, Harbor, Mountain(s), Ocean, Panoramic, Trees/Woods","True","https://brokerageengine.s3.amazonaws.com/listing-media/vistasir/1728509408865_1080p-1939-Jaybrook-Dr--Rancho-Palos-Verdes-Ca_UNBRANDED.mov","","Bay Window(s), Blinds, Drapes, Garden Window(s)","1950","90275","2042","RPRS-4*"
